  Child content is rendered inside the component. To fill a named slot of the
  component, set `slot="name"` on the child element.

  ## Events

  Each `on_*` attribute takes the name of a LiveView event and requires an `id`.
  The LiveView receives `%{"detail" => ..., "value" => ..., "id" => ...}`.

    * `on_header_cell_sort` - The name of the custom event fired before a new sort direction is set upon a user gesture. Cancellation of this event stops the user-initiated change in sort direction.
    * `on_search` - input The name of the custom event fired during search bar input
    * `on_change_selection_all` - The name of the custom event fired before header row is selected/unselected upon a user gesture.
    * `on_row_change_selection` - The name of the custom event fired before a row is selected/unselected upon a user gesture.
    * `on_batch_actions_cancel_clicked` - The name of the custom event fired after the Cancel button is clicked.
    * `on_row_expando_toggled` - The name of the custom event fired after the expanded state of a row is toggled upon a user gesture.
    * `on_row_selected` - The name of the custom event fired after a row has been selected.
    * `on_row_all_selected` - The name of the custom event fired after all rows have been selected.
    * `on_sorted` - The name of the custom event fired after the table has been sorted.
    * `on_filtered` - The name of the custom event fired after the table has been filtered containing remaining rows.
  """
  attr :rest, :global, doc: "any additional HTML attributes, e.g. `class`, `id`, `slot`, `phx-*`"

  attr :batch_expansion, :boolean,
    default: nil,
    doc: "`true` if this table should support batch expansion Carbon default: `false`."

  attr :expandable, :boolean,
    default: nil,
    doc: "Specify whether the rows should be able to be expandable Carbon default: `false`."

  attr :filter_rows, :any,
    default: nil,
